  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Building Training Development.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Red R UK - lead provider. The British Council is seeking a supplier to support the initial development of a suite of Monitoring and Evaluation (M&amp;E) training courses.  The aim of these courses is to professionalise evaluation through the provision of technical evaluation training courses. The objective of the procured courses will be to support and enable regional and programme staff who need to understand and apply monitoring or evaluation skills in their work.  As the British Council has been through a transformation process, there are staff members in new roles who need to be informed users of evaluation products, as well as oversee and ensure the delivery of quality data on their programme work.  This contract will be to scope, design, and build the initial M&amp;E course offerings. Ideally these initial courses should be &#x201c;self-pacing&#x201d;&#x2014;e.g. users are able to access them independently on an &#x201c;as needed&#x201d; basis or specific schedule, without the need for ongoing expert support or trainer delivery.  Given the British Council&#x2019;s global team, the courses will likely need to be online.</narrative>
  </description>
